course: dictionary
lesson: 8377
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «It is the end of summer: green had given way to gold in the fields, and rowans were reddening.» Rowans here are trees, because the fields and the reddening show you that the writer means plants, not people.
explain: Rowan can also be a name, a first name for boys and girls. A name starts with a capital letter even in the middle of a sentence, so a capital R is a clue that Rowan is a person.
explain: Ask yourself what the word is pointing to. A rowan tree has feathery leaves and bunches of bright red-orange berries in autumn, and it is also called a mountain ash. If the sentence talks about berries, leaves or branches, it is the tree.
fact: A rowan is a small tree with feathery leaves.
fact: Rowan berries are bright red-orange and grow in bunches in autumn.
fact: A rowan is also called a mountain ash.
fact: Birds eat rowan berries in autumn.
fact: In folklore in Scotland and Ireland, a rowan near a house was said to keep away witches.
exercise: «Rowans were reddening» in the fields. What is a rowan here? | A kind of green field | *A small tree with bright red-orange berries | A bird that sings at dawn | A lake in the hills
exercise: Which sentence uses Rowan as a first name? | The rowan dropped red berries on the path. | *Rowan ran to catch the bus. | The rowan stood by the gate. | Birds ate the rowan berries.
exercise: In which season do birds eat rowan berries? | Summer | Winter | *Autumn | Spring
test: «Rowan dropped her pencil and laughed.» What does Rowan mean here? | A bunch of berries | A kind of bird | A tree with red berries | *A first name for a person
test: What is another name for a rowan tree? | Oak | Pine | Holly | *Mountain ash
exam: In «Rowan planted a rowan by the door», what does the second rowan mean? | A bird | A first name | *A small tree with red berries | A door
